reen's theorem to evaluate $\\oint_C(e^{-x^2}-x^2y)\\,dx+(y+xy^2)\\,dy,$ where $C$ is the counterclockwise boundary of the disk with polar description $0\\le r\\le 1,\\ 0\\le\\theta\\le2\\pi$." 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562773 1072 #uuid "36d37f77-94a1-5750-955e-00c0cfbaff25" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562773 1074 "Green's theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\oint_C P\\,dx+Q\\,dy=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,dA.\n$$\n\nIn our case, the region $D$ and its boundary $C$ satisfy the conditions of Green's theorem:\n\n![](images/ee/eed043488a6cd3949da95907125dcdfa2f946feefff60772495e48e9610c4bc1.png)\n\nNow, since\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=e^{-x^2}-x^2y,\\quad Q(x,y)=y+xy^2,\n$$\n\nwe have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}=- x^{2},\\quad \\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}=y^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying Green's theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\oint_C(e^{-x^2}-x^2y)\\,dx+(y+xy^2)\\,dy&=\\iint_D\\left(\\frac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x}-\\frac{\\partial P}{\\partial y}\\right)\\,dA \\\\ &=\\iint_D\\left(y^{2}-(- x^{2})\\right)\\,dA \\\\ &=\\iint_D (x^2+y^2)\\,dA.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the region $D$ can be represented in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\le r\\le 1,0\\le\\theta\\le 2 \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nThe change of variables formula for plane polar coordinates states that\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,dA=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate our double integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D (x^2+y^2)\\,dA&=\\iint_\\Delta (r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta))\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{1}r^3(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\int_{0}^{1}r^3\\,dr\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left[\\frac{r^4}{4}\\right]_{0}^{1}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\left(\\frac{1}{4}-0\\right)\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{2 \\pi}\\frac{1}{4}\\,d\\theta \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}[\\theta]_{0}^{2 \\pi} \\\\ &=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(2 \\pi-0\\right) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\pi}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562774 1080 "54 \\pi" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562774 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562774 1083 #uuid "39a9a9d6-02ad-5f5b-ba6e-05886838a7e2" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562775 1080 "162 \\pi" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562775 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562775 1083 #uuid "3b9caf01-baab-5870-b7d6-820bbcfe7d91" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562774 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562778 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562797 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562809 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1075 #edb/ref 17592186562812 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1077 "selection" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1078 #edb/ref 17592186562809 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562776 1079 #uuid "419fba28-082c-5d89-8e47-9823b5bee043" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562777 1080 "\\frac{35 \\pi}{6}" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562777 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562777 1083 #uuid "4f1bf688-5389-548e-93fa-5d1ff024bc7f" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562778 1080 "- \\frac{243 \\pi}{2}" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562778 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562778 1083 #uuid "5195a77d-03e2-5c78-823d-910cf0023ca6" 13194139536061 17592186045443 true] [17592186562779 10